Germany operates world's highest-performing deposit return scheme achieving 98% recovery on single-use bottles/cans. Consumers pay 8-25 cent deposits (Einweg bottles) or EUR 1.50 for bottle crates (Mehrweg), refundable at supermarket Pfandautomaten or manually at checkout. Multi-use bottles (Mehrweg) refill 50+ cycles. After return, bottles are recycled via reverse vending machines into new containers or reused if Mehrweg. This dual-track system (reuse + recycling) balances circular recovery with infrastructure investment, demonstrating deposit systems' effectiveness when combined with return convenience and producer participation.